Study #13: "Timing of antiretroviral therapy after diagnosis of cryptococcal meningitis"
- Decision: INCLUDE
- Confidence: HIGH
- Rationale: This is a well-designed RCT that directly addresses the review question. It randomized 177 HIV-infected 
adults with cryptococcal meningitis to either early ART (1-2 weeks after diagnosis) or deferred ART (5 weeks after 
diagnosis). The study reports mortality at 26 weeks as the primary outcome and found significantly higher mortality with
earlier ART initiation (45% vs 30%, HR 1.73, p=0.03). This study meets ALL selection criteria.

